# AEGIS-COGNITION Cursor Entry Point

For every request in this repository, apply `$software-engineering-constitution` with
proportional rigor. Use the full engineering workflow for implementation, review,
testing, architecture, security, reliability, performance, release, and production
readiness; for simple requests, still state material assumptions, avoid unsupported
claims, verify when needed, and distinguish VERIFIED from NOT VERIFIED.

The canonical repository copy is `docs/ENGINEERING_CONSTITUTION.md`; keep it aligned
with the canonical local source file named `Ultimate Software Engineering Constitution
— Maximum-Rigor Prompt.md`.

Always apply `docs/archive/reports/system-prompt.md` when creating or modifying AEGIS plugins, tools, skills, or actions.

Keep explicit test scratch directories inside `.local/tmp/<unique-run-id>`.
Never create AEGIS test directories directly under the user's home directory.
Do not share pytest basetemp directories across concurrent runs; pytest can remove
their contents. Caches and quarantine belong in `.local/`, which is excluded from
Git and Docker. Historical reports and source snapshots belong in `docs/archive/`.

For plugin work, the default stance is zero trust:

- typed Rust or schema-checked boundaries only
- least-privilege host capabilities
- explicit R0-R4 policy classification
- approval or staging gates for R3/R4
- BLAKE3-bound physical evidence
- deterministic execution with host-injected time, entropy, IDs, and external state

Prefer the native Cursor rule at `.cursor/rules/aegis-zero-trust-plugin-creator.mdc` and the agent `.cursor/agents/aegis-zero-trust-plugin-architect.md` for detailed workflow.
